================================================================================
Apache-2.0 derived works (Adobe React Spectrum)
================================================================================

The following packages are SolidJS ports of, and contain code derived from,
Adobe's React Spectrum project:

  @proyecto-viviana/solid-stately         derived from  @react-stately/*
  @proyecto-viviana/solidaria             derived from  @react-aria/*
  @proyecto-viviana/solidaria-components  derived from  react-aria-components
  @proyecto-viviana/solid-spectrum        derived from  @react-spectrum/s2
  @proyecto-viviana/ui                    derived from  @react-spectrum/s2,
                                           with local additions

Original work:
  React Spectrum
  Copyright 2019 Adobe (and other contributors)
  https://github.com/adobe/react-spectrum
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Significant changes (Apache-2.0 section 4(b)): the source has been ported from
React to SolidJS. APIs, the reactivity model (signals/stores in place of hooks),
rendering, and behavior have been adapted to Solid's primitives.

Some source files identify candidate or verified upstream mappings with an
upstream notice or a "Ported from" / "Based on" reference. The repository is
still auditing exact per-file mappings. This project-level notice does not claim
that the per-file audit is complete.

This product also depends on, or bundles for reference, the following Apache-2.0
material from Adobe:

  - @react-spectrum/s2, @adobe/spectrum-tokens, and
    @internationalized/{date,number,string} (runtime / peer dependencies).
  - A vendored copy of the React Spectrum S2 documentation site under
    apps/comparison/vendor/s2-docs/, used as a comparison reference. That
    directory carries its own upstream NOTICE at
    apps/comparison/vendor/s2-docs/NOTICE.

